# Keep the knowledge graph about SOURCE, not build output.
#
# Why this file exists: graphify walks the tree and extracts an AST per file.
# Minified bundles extract as thousands of one-letter functions, so the graph's
# "god nodes" came out as `n()`, `r()`, `e()` — the report was structurally
# useless and the node count (22.9k) blew past the 5k HTML-viz limit.
#
# graphify already honours .gitignore, which covers `public/assets/`,
# `landing/dist/` and — since the demo stopped being a tracked snapshot —
# `landing/public/app/` too. The entry below is kept anyway: the directory is
# still on disk after every `build:site`, it was the bulk of the god-node noise,
# and a rule that survives a change of ignore file costs nothing.

# Build output of the client app that the landing site serves as its demo.
landing/public/app/

# Vendored minified libraries — bundled third-party code, not our source.
**/*.min.js

# Bundler output, wherever a build happens to land it.
**/dist/

# Lockfiles: large, churny, and contribute no structure to a code graph.
**/bun.lock

# graphify's own output, so a rebuild never re-ingests the previous graph.
graphify-out/
